  "title": "Sampling, isolating and identifying microplastics ingested by fish and invertebrates",
  "abstract": "Microplastic debris (<5 mm) is a prolific environmental pollutant, found worldwide in marine, freshwater and terrestrial ecosystems. This review assesses the numerous different methods used to identify microplastics ingested by marine organisms.",
